(6881510, 1035939, 20799, '<td valign="top">The collision of Uranus and Neptune - this was one of my favorites. I loved the array of red screams in between. <br/>Good job and a unique take on the challenge.</td>', 'The collision of Uranus and Neptune - this was one of my favorites. I loved the array of red screams in between. Good job and a unique take on the challenge.', '2012-10-12 05:17:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6881515, 1036216, 100393, '<td valign="top">Congratulations (again!!) - It is indicative of the quality of your work and your dedication that all of your profile pics (even with 9 showing) are 8+ scores.<br/> <br/>I always look for (and look forward to) the-Gyaban-entry in these challenges.<br/> <br/>I''d love to see what you''d come up with for a month-long Expert challenge. Have we ever had one?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-10-12 05:00:52.</i></td>', 'Congratulations (again!!) - It is indicative of the quality of your work and your dedication that all of your profile pics (even with 9 showing) are 8+ scores. I always look for (and look forward to) the-Gyaban-entry in these challenges. I''d love to see what you''d come up with for a month-long Expert challenge. Have we ever had one?', '2012-10-12 06:00:40.000000', '2012-10-12 06:00:52.000000', 0),
(6881525, 1036216, 114969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Paul:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations (again!!) - It is indicative of the quality of your work and your dedication that all of your profile pics (even with 9 showing) are 8+ scores.<br/> <br/>I always look for (and look forward to) the-Gyaban-entry in these challenges.<br/> <br/>I''d love to see what you''d come up with for a month-long Expert challenge. Have we ever had one? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks a lot Paul. At least <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/challenge_results.php?CHALLENGE_ID=1457" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">one challenge</a> was a month-long expert one, but it sure would be very interesting to have another one.</td>', 'Originally posted by Paul: Congratulations (again!!) - It is indicative of the quality of your work and your dedication that all of your profile pics (even with 9 showing) are 8+ scores. I always look for (and look forward to) the-Gyaban-entry in these challenges. I''d love to see what you''d come up with for a month-long Expert challenge. Have we ever had one?   Thanks a lot Paul. At least one challenge was a month-long expert one, but it sure would be very interesting to have another one.', '2012-10-12 06:12:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(6881540, 1036216, 114285, '<td valign="top">It was the beams of light that got my attention!</td>', 'It was the beams of light that got my attention!', '2012-10-12 06:59:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(6881545, 1036226, 72318, '<td valign="top">Statue of liberty has no "weight" in the scene, it is like it is cut out and stuck there (the left hand side blend is all wrong considering the lighting and background shadows/highlight)... that might explain some of the low votes (i didnt vote) as the whole effect is ruined by the jarring nature of the statue which doesnt quite "live" there - not to say you werent the only offender in this challenge but these things do count...  that you got some 10''s and 9''s it testament to the quality of the rest of the composition - in fact it may have done better without the statue (less is more...)</td>', 'Statue of liberty has no "weight" in the scene, it is like it is cut out and stuck there (the left hand side blend is all wrong considering the lighting and background shadows/highlight)... that might explain some of the low votes (i didnt vote) as the whole effect is ruined by the jarring nature of the statue which doesnt quite "live" there - not to say you werent the only offender in this challenge but these things do count...  that you got some 10''s and 9''s it testament to the quality of the rest of the composition - in fact it may have done better without the statue (less is more...)', '2012-10-12 07:10:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(6881553, 1036226, 109387, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by inshaala:</b></div><hr/><i> Statue of liberty has no "weight" in the scene, it is like it is cut out and stuck there (the left hand side blend is all wrong considering the lighting and background shadows/highlight)... that might explain some of the low votes (i didnt vote) as the whole effect is ruined by the jarring nature of the statue which doesnt quite "live" there - not to say you werent the only offender in this challenge but these things do count...  that you got some 10''s and 9''s it testament to the quality of the rest of the composition - in fact it may have done better without the statue (less is more...) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I was surely not happy with the blending result of the statue. I left it as the last thing to fix, but it was late to properly think about its blending. But I couldn''t get rid of it since it was the engine of the my main idea. Still I don''t think that the blending of the statue can be the reason for receving a lot of 1s, since I can see the vast majority of the other entries very poorly edited, so one element can be the reason for this voting. I surely agree that most of the time ''less I more''... I should never forget it!</td>', 'Originally posted by inshaala: Statue of liberty has no "weight" in the scene, it is like it is cut out and stuck there (the left hand side blend is all wrong considering the lighting and background shadows/highlight)... that might explain some of the low votes (i didnt vote) as the whole effect is ruined by the jarring nature of the statue which doesnt quite "live" there - not to say you werent the only offender in this challenge but these things do count...  that you got some 10''s and 9''s it testament to the quality of the rest of the composition - in fact it may have done better without the statue (less is more...)   I was surely not happy with the blending result of the statue. I left it as the last thing to fix, but it was late to properly think about its blending. But I couldn''t get rid of it since it was the engine of the my main idea. Still I don''t think that the blending of the statue can be the reason for receving a lot of 1s, since I can see the vast majority of the other entries very poorly edited, so one element can be the reason for this voting. I surely agree that most of the time ''less I more''... I should never forget it!', '2012-10-12 07:19:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6881568, 1035912, 114969, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Frank! I really like how you managed the depth of field, it''s the attention to such details that makes composites more realistic. The choice of the beach is also very good: white sand would have much less impact obviously. Happy to see you''re having fun experimenting :-)</td>', 'Congratulations Frank! I really like how you managed the depth of field, it''s the attention to such details that makes composites more realistic. The choice of the beach is also very good: white sand would have much less impact obviously. Happy to see you''re having fun experimenting :-)', '2012-10-12 08:26:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(6881569, 1036219, 114969, '<td valign="top">Very, very nice Lydia! I really like that one. The place was worth the search, it works greatly in that challenge. The light beams also help to render a dusty atmosphere, and the bones are just creepy :-) Congratulations.</td>', 'Very, very nice Lydia! I really like that one. The place was worth the search, it works greatly in that challenge. The light beams also help to render a dusty atmosphere, and the bones are just creepy :-) Congratulations.', '2012-10-12 08:28:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(6881570, 1035626, 114969, '<td valign="top">Very nice John. Dark and creepy, muddy colors, perfect. I even love the grain, and wish there was some on the ''man part'' too! Your work is a great source of inspiration, and you show here the versatility of your talent. Congrats.</td>', 'Very nice John. Dark and creepy, muddy colors, perfect. I even love the grain, and wish there was some on the ''man part'' too! Your work is a great source of inspiration, and you show here the versatility of your talent. Congrats.', '2012-10-12 08:39:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(6881572, 1036226, 114969, '<td valign="top">I really wish you had some more time to polish this one (especially the statue). I am convinced it has a great potential, as the general mood and colors work brilliantly together. The sky is superb too. Moreover, the caravan is fantastic, I really like this exile in the middle of nowhere. You need to find a way to make your baby sleep more ;-)</td>', 'I really wish you had some more time to polish this one (especially the statue). I am convinced it has a great potential, as the general mood and colors work brilliantly together. The sky is superb too. Moreover, the caravan is fantastic, I really like this exile in the middle of nowhere. You need to find a way to make your baby sleep more ;-)', '2012-10-12 08:49:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(6881573, 1035939, 113278, '<td valign="top">Sadly underrated, this is a wonderful abstract and managed a 9 from me</td>', 'Sadly underrated, this is a wonderful abstract and managed a 9 from me', '2012-10-12 08:49:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(6881579, 1036216, 82707, '<td valign="top">Amazing image! ....as usual!  Congrats on a well deserved ''Blue'', Christophe!  There is always the story, and then there is the image.  Thank you for sharing your amazingly, fabulous ''talent''.  You are an exceptional artist &amp; photographer.....  Do I care if you fit into a pigeon hole.... not remotely..... Thank you for choosing to share your fabulous talent on this site!  It is one of the reasons that I am still a member.  (Oh! ...and there is more than, a little, image envy)  LOL! :)</td>', 'Amazing image! ....as usual!  Congrats on a well deserved ''Blue'', Christophe!  There is always the story, and then there is the image.  Thank you for sharing your amazingly, fabulous ''talent''.  You are an exceptional artist & photographer.....  Do I care if you fit into a pigeon hole.... not remotely..... Thank you for choosing to share your fabulous talent on this site!  It is one of the reasons that I am still a member.  (Oh! ...and there is more than, a little, image envy)  LOL! :)', '2012-10-12 09:11:45.000000', NULL, 0),
